# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials
#
# The Supabase service-role key bypasses Row-Level Security entirely. This
# repository is public, so a key that reaches its history can only be remedied
# by rotating the key — deleting the commit does not reach forks or caches.
# Keep every credential in .env.local, which is never committed.
#
# No env file is committed at all, .env.example included. A template with
# empty values still names every credential the project uses, and the one
# thing a public repository should not publish is a checklist of what to
# go looking for.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase CLI local state
#
# .temp/ holds the linked project ref and CLI scratch state; .branches/ holds
# local branch databases. Neither belongs in version control.
# Migrations and config.toml DO belong in version control.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies and build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
build/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code local state
#
# settings.local.json holds machine-specific permissions/paths; .mcp.json
# (if added) can carry credentials. commands/ and skills/ are shared and
# belong in version control.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
.mcp.json

# Session artifacts — context-usage dumps written to the repo root by name,
# e.g. 2026-08-28-034747-context-usage.txt. Diagnostics about a session, not
# about the project.
*-context-usage.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credential hardening
#
# These paths do not exist yet. The rules precede them deliberately — an ignore
# rule only protects a file it was written before.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Private keys and certificates (config.toml references ../certs/my-key.pem)
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
certs/

# Supabase JWT signing keys — config.toml: "DO NOT commit your signing keys file"
signing_keys.json
**/signing_keys.json

# Tool credentials
.envrc
.npmrc
.netrc
.pgpass

# Expo and editor local state
.expo/
.vscode/settings.json
